{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/25758-are-any-of-the-city-by-night-books-worthwhile-material-for-a-mage-game","id":25758,"title":"Are any of the City: By Night books worthwhile material for a Mage game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-08T06:09:00-08:00","id":25758,"title":"Are any of the City: By Night books worthwhile material for a Mage game?","content":"It seems the only setting book that Mage ever got was The Fallen Tower: Las Vegas, and it came so late, that it makes me wonder if there isn't some decent Mage content hidden away in one of the By Night books. <br /> <br /> If not, why do you think Mage only ever saw the one book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T09:19:37-08:00","id":25833,"title":"","content":"There's something in Looms of Fate and Chaos Factor... but not much...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T03:21:20-08:00","id":27099,"title":"","content":"Most of the setting stuff for Mage seems to be in the fluff scattered throughout the system books so you have to go and piece it together instead of it collected into a lot of scenario books like the other games usually have. A lot of the actual settings books were not in normal places, like Mage Chronicles was mainly places in the Umbra and Digital Web for instance. There is also Bitter Road and a few others if I recall correctly.<br /> <br /> Chicago by Night has a little Mage stuff in it if I remember correctly though not a lot of it is direct; one in particular is that one of the Tremere is heavily involved in a Mage mailing list (they think she is a sorceress with an academic knowledge of blood magic) who is a concern to some of the other vampires since her extensive communications with Mages could lead to trouble. A natural for that would be if the other vampires intimidate her into being quiet on the list and a Mage or Mages deciding to stop in to see if she is alright.<br /> <br /> Of course it is possible to run Mage games using the city information and infer plots from what the vampires are doing without actually bringing the Mages and Vampires in contact with each other too. I did that with both Chicago by Night and DC by Night in several campaigns, and in one of them that revolved around a band whose members were Mages the Succubus Club was a fairly regular gig and the goings on in and around the club were good targets for amateur investigations of the band members.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T09:08:25-08:00","id":27237,"title":"","content":"There's a small amount in DC by Night and an interesting Mage hook in Milwaukee. Otherwise, not really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T10:18:30-08:00","id":27284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/25758-are-any-of-the-city-by-night-books-worthwhile-material-for-a-mage-game#post25758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If not, why do you think Mage only ever saw the one book?</div> </div> </div> </div>1e Mage wasn't that long and didn't have a chance to really get into it.<br /> <br /> 2e Mage was a bit more focused on the far away places (either around the world or off it) Mages could get to; so there's way more books about those than specific cities.<br /> <br /> Rev. Mage was, again, fairly short in comparison and By Night books weren't as focused on in Revised in general.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T08:34:15-08:00","id":33222,"title":"","content":"For my own campaign set in Chicago I found the NWoD Chicago book to be an excellent source of ideas in that it covered local legends, places of spiritual significance and enough generically magical/spiritual elements (not to mention maps and descriptions of locations in the city that are only a decade out of date instead of nearly a quarter-century out of date). While the NWoD stats and setting specific stuff (i.e. the NewMage factions) the side-bars and everything else made it more than worth it for me.<br /> <br /> While I haven't personally checked it out, I suspect the NWoD Boston supplement would be similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}